    {
      "date": "2026-10-16",
      "source": "Wikimedia Commons geosearch (120 m around each junction)",
      "result": "tourist/building photos; J1 clock-tower set (File:Tour de l'Horloge du centre-ville de Tunis 01..06.jpg, CC0, taken 2025-10-02) shows a signalised pedestrian crossing at the roundabout but no countable lane markings; no other photo shows an approach at the stop line; no lane count verified"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-17",
      "source": "Mapillary (graph.mapillary.com, user-supplied token; token not stored)",
      "result": "445 image hits (junction boxes overlap, so some images count twice), all 2015/2018 except 18 from 2020-08-21 near J3; matching photos for 19 of 30 way-directions, none for 26242831 (both), 33803062, 39170210 at J4, 56065135, 95132613 exit, 106509679, 306643020 (both), 545291183, 704802731 approach. All are handheld phone shots through a windscreen. On 18 of the 19 matched directions the carriageway near the junction shows no lane-divider paint, or the view is blocked or turning, so no lane count can be read at the stop line. The only countable markings: 10641416 (OSM lanes=2) shows one dashed divider = 2 marked lanes about 30 m past J1 (391454508600365 on 2018-05-27, 813444632625851 on 2018-05-26); the way is 316 m and uniformity is not confirmed, so it stays osm_tagged. No lane count verified. Incidental observations (2018): signal heads at the J1 roundabout entries from Avenue Mohamed V and the roundabout (500700031128096, 325457825591789); zebra crossings with stop lines on the J6 Rue d'Alger and Avenue Habib Bourguiba approaches (599754087650398, 241702187743440, 582172526508230); tram tracks embedded in Avenue Habib Thameur at J4/J5 (2592441237723578, 2863940113817511); no bus-only lane markings seen.",
      "query": "images within 80 m of each junction; per way-direction: on the way (<14 m offset), 8-90 m from the junction, camera heading within 35 deg of travel"
    },
    {
